window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b286-c446009b018d6d8b.json"]={sha256:"c446009b018d6d8bcb466e0a13aaca32633743a760e2807034e9eecd5f2fc6b4",value:{"id":"b286","title":"離岸潛堤地形整合","titleEn":"Submerged-breakwater coastal integration","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"連結潛堤越頂透射缺口流與海岸地形的相互作用。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Connect submerged-breakwater transmission, gap currents and evolving coastal morphology. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["淹水深與共同基準","Submergence and shared datum"],["破波水深尺度","Depth-limited breaking scale"],["規則波能通量","Regular-wave energy flux"],["淺水傳播時間","Shallow-water propagation time"],["數值步長與收斂","Numerical timestep and convergence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["淹水深與共同基準","破波水深尺度","規則波能通量","淺水傳播時間","數值步長與收斂"],"labelsEn":["Submergence and shared datum","Depth-limited breaking scale","Regular-wave energy flux","Shallow-water propagation time","Numerical timestep and convergence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。假設水位由2.0升至2.2m、堤頂仍1.2m，覆水0.8增至1.0m，增加25%；相同1.6m入射波的相對覆水由0.50變0.625，仍不能推出新的透射量。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission. Raising level from2.0 to2.2m at fixed crest1.2m increases cover from0.8 to1.0m by25%. Relative cover at unchanged1.6m incident height changes from0.50 to0.625, without determining a new transmission coefficient. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b286-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「淹水深與共同基準」與「波高與能量透射」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Submergence and shared datum\" and \"Wave-height and energy transmission\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-01","title":"淹水深與共同基準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「淹水深與共同基準」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Submergence and shared datum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。潮汐、增水與沉陷會改變相對淹水深，使同一結構在不同時段呈現不同透流狀態；越頂自由面和波浪運動仍須另行解析，不能把水下高度直接視為減波量。 假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「淹水深與共同基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone. Tide, surge and settlement change relative cover, so the same structure experiences different transmission states. The overtopping free surface and wave motion still need separate analysis; water cover cannot directly represent the amount of wave reduction or the resulting shoreline response. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Submergence and shared datum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「淹水深與共同基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Submergence and shared datum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-01-k1","title":"淹水深與共同基準","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum","text":"潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。潮汐、增水與沉陷會改變相對淹水深，使同一結構在不同時段呈現不同透流狀態；越頂自由面和波浪運動仍須另行解析，不能把水下高度直接視為減波量。","textEn":"Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone. Tide, surge and settlement change relative cover, so the same structure experiences different transmission states.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「淹水深與共同基準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Submergence and shared datum\" is correct?","options":["相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。","潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.","Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b286-v15-02","title":"淹水深與共同基準：定量估算","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「淹水深與共同基準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Submergence and shared datum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「淹水深與共同基準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Submergence and shared datum\", which statement holds?","options":["缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b286-v15-03","title":"淹水深與共同基準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「淹水深與共同基準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Submergence and shared datum” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。","observationEn":"Site practice: Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section.","failure":"注意干擾：不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。","textEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。","textEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「淹水深與共同基準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Submergence and shared datum\"?","options":["將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b286-v15-04","title":"淹水深與共同基準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「淹水深與共同基準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Submergence and shared datum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。局部低點若未量到，也可能集中越頂流而造成後側沖刷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. An unmeasured low point may also concentrate overtopping flow and cause localized scour behind the structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。局部低點若未量到，也可能集中越頂流而造成後側沖刷。","textEn":"Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. An unmeasured low point may also concentrate overtopping flow and cause localized scour behind the structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「淹水深與共同基準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Submergence and shared datum\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b286-v15-05","title":"波高與能量透射：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「波高與能量透射」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wave-height and energy transmission” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。量測必須分離入射反射及透射成分，兩側頻譜也可能因破波而改變；只有明定波型與能量定義後，才可比較堤前與堤後的水理量。 假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波高與能量透射」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth. Measurements must separate incident, reflected and transmitted components, and breaking can change the spectrum. Only after defining wave type and energy consistently can measurements on either side be compared; an amplitude percentage is not automatically an energy percentage. Assume Hi=2m and Ht=0.8m, giving Kt=0.40. Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave-height and energy transmission” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「波高與能量透射」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave-height and energy transmission”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-05-k1","title":"波高與能量透射","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission","text":"透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。量測必須分離入射反射及透射成分，兩側頻譜也可能因破波而改變；只有明定波型與能量定義後，才可比較堤前與堤後的水理量。","textEn":"Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth. Measurements must separate incident, reflected and transmitted components, and breaking can change the spectrum.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波高與能量透射」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wave-height and energy transmission\" is correct?","options":["波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。"],"optionsEn":["A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b286-v15-06","title":"波高與能量透射：定量估算","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波高與能量透射」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wave-height and energy transmission” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume Hi=2m and Ht=0.8m, giving Kt=0.40. Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume Hi=2m and Ht=0.8m, giving Kt=0.40. Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波高與能量透射」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wave-height and energy transmission\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b286-v15-07","title":"波高與能量透射：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「波高與能量透射」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wave-height and energy transmission” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors.","failure":"注意干擾：把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。","textEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。","textEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波高與能量透射」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wave-height and energy transmission\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height."],"answer":1,"explanation":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b286-v15-08","title":"波高與能量透射：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波高與能量透射」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wave-height and energy transmission” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。即使整體透射降低，缺口附近仍可能有局部高波。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. Lower overall transmission can still coexist with locally high waves near a gap in the breakwater. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。即使整體透射降低，缺口附近仍可能有局部高波。","textEn":"Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. Lower overall transmission can still coexist with locally high waves near a gap in the breakwater.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波高與能量透射」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wave-height and energy transmission\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b286-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「破波水深尺度」與「缺口連續流量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Depth-limited breaking scale\" and \"Gap-flow continuity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-09","title":"破波水深尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「破波水深尺度」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Depth-limited breaking scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。潛堤頂部流速和波形會改變，短堤頂也未必達到平衡破波；教學比例應用於辨識量級，不能被當成任何不規則波條件下的固定上限。 假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破波水深尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations. Crest currents and wave shape change over a submerged structure, and a short crest may not develop equilibrium breaking. A teaching ratio establishes scale rather than a universal ceiling for every irregular-wave condition. Assume a selected breaker indexγb=0.78 at depth2m. Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Depth-limited breaking scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破波水深尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Depth-limited breaking scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-09-k1","title":"破波水深尺度","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale","text":"淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。潛堤頂部流速和波形會改變，短堤頂也未必達到平衡破波；教學比例應用於辨識量級，不能被當成任何不規則波條件下的固定上限。","textEn":"Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations. Crest currents and wave shape change over a submerged structure, and a short crest may not develop equilibrium breaking.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破波水深尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Depth-limited breaking scale\" is correct?","options":["淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b286-v15-10","title":"破波水深尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破波水深尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Depth-limited breaking scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a selected breaker indexγb=0.78 at depth2m. Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a selected breaker indexγb=0.78 at depth2m. Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破波水深尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Depth-limited breaking scale\", which statement holds?","options":["希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b286-v15-11","title":"破波水深尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破波水深尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Depth-limited breaking scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas.","failure":"注意干擾：水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。","textEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。","textEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破波水深尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Depth-limited breaking scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。","在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.","Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b286-v15-12","title":"破波水深尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破波水深尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Depth-limited breaking scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。若一直使用同一破波位置和係數，後側波況與岸灘受力可能被系統性低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. Keeping the same breaking point and coefficient can systematically understate lee-side waves and beach exposure during higher water. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。若一直使用同一破波位置和係數，後側波況與岸灘受力可能被系統性低估。","textEn":"Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. Keeping the same breaking point and coefficient can systematically understate lee-side waves and beach exposure during higher water.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破波水深尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Depth-limited breaking scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b286-v15-13","title":"缺口連續流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「缺口連續流量」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gap-flow continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。面積平均流速只能滿足連續方程，不代表最大紊流或近床速度；流向會隨潮波改變，分析需要把堤段越頂輸入與缺口排出放在同一收支框架。 假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「缺口連續流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure. Section-mean velocity satisfies continuity but is not the maximum turbulent or near-bed velocity. Direction changes with tides and waves, so crest inflow and gap outflow must be evaluated within one water budget rather than as unrelated local observations. Assume steady gap discharge30m³/s through effective area20m². Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gap-flow continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「缺口連續流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gap-flow continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-13-k1","title":"缺口連續流量","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity","text":"堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。面積平均流速只能滿足連續方程，不代表最大紊流或近床速度；流向會隨潮波改變，分析需要把堤段越頂輸入與缺口排出放在同一收支框架。","textEn":"Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure. Section-mean velocity satisfies continuity but is not the maximum turbulent or near-bed velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺口連續流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gap-flow continuity\" is correct?","options":["缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。","堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。"],"optionsEn":["The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.","Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b286-v15-14","title":"缺口連續流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「缺口連續流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gap-flow continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume steady gap discharge30m³/s through effective area20m². Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume steady gap discharge30m³/s through effective area20m². Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「缺口連續流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gap-flow continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b286-v15-15","title":"缺口連續流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「缺口連續流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gap-flow continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section.","failure":"注意干擾：斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。","textEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。","textEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「缺口連續流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gap-flow continuity\"?","options":["沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b286-v15-16","title":"缺口連續流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「缺口連續流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gap-flow continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。若儀器只放在緩流區，收支殘差會掩蓋真正的集中流和沖刷熱點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. Instruments placed only in slow water conceal concentrated currents and scour hotspots behind apparently modest mean-flow observations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。若儀器只放在緩流區，收支殘差會掩蓋真正的集中流和沖刷熱點。","textEn":"Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. Instruments placed only in slow water conceal concentrated currents and scour hotspots behind apparently modest mean-flow observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「缺口連續流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gap-flow continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b286-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「規則波能通量」與「床面剪力無因次化」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Regular-wave energy flux\" and \"Dimensionless bed shear\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-17","title":"規則波能通量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「規則波能通量」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Regular-wave energy flux” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。群速度傳遞能量而相速度描述波峰移動，混用會改變功率；入射角、反射和耗散也影響垂直結構方向的能流，單位寬度結果不能直接當成整座結構承受的總負荷。 假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「規則波能通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ. Group velocity transports energy while phase velocity follows crests. Incidence, reflection and dissipation also affect the normal energy flux, so a result per unit crest width does not directly describe total structural loading or impact pressure. Assume a regular linear wave:ρ=1025kg/m³, H=2m, Cg=5m/s. E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Regular-wave energy flux” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「規則波能通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Regular-wave energy flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-17-k1","title":"規則波能通量","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux","text":"波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。群速度傳遞能量而相速度描述波峰移動，混用會改變功率；入射角、反射和耗散也影響垂直結構方向的能流，單位寬度結果不能直接當成整座結構承受的總負荷。","textEn":"Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ. Group velocity transports energy while phase velocity follows crests.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「規則波能通量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Regular-wave energy flux\" is correct?","options":["規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。"],"optionsEn":["Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b286-v15-18","title":"規則波能通量：定量估算","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「規則波能通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Regular-wave energy flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a regular linear wave:ρ=1025kg/m³, H=2m, Cg=5m/s. E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a regular linear wave:ρ=1025kg/m³, H=2m, Cg=5m/s. E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「規則波能通量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Regular-wave energy flux\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b286-v15-19","title":"規則波能通量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「規則波能通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Regular-wave energy flux” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient.","failure":"注意干擾：使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。","textEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。","textEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「規則波能通量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Regular-wave energy flux\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b286-v15-20","title":"規則波能通量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「規則波能通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Regular-wave energy flux” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。數值即使量綱正確，仍可能因統計定義不同而不可比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. Dimensionally correct numbers may still be incomparable because the underlying statistical definition is different. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。數值即使量綱正確，仍可能因統計定義不同而不可比較。","textEn":"Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. Dimensionally correct numbers may still be incomparable because the underlying statistical definition is different.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規則波能通量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Regular-wave energy flux\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b286-v15-21","title":"床面剪力無因次化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「床面剪力無因次化」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dimensionless bed shear” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。希爾茲參數只把作用力無因次化，起動條件還受級配、床面形態與振盪流影響；不能由單一參數宣告侵蝕深度，亦不能跳過黏性細料與非黏性砂的不同機制。 假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「床面剪力無因次化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale. The Shields parameter nondimensionalizes forcing; onset also depends on grading, bed form and oscillatory motion. One parameter does not give scour depth, and cohesive fines require a different treatment from the noncohesive grains assumed here. Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dimensionless bed shear” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「床面剪力無因次化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dimensionless bed shear”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-21-k1","title":"床面剪力無因次化","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear","text":"潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。希爾茲參數只把作用力無因次化，起動條件還受級配、床面形態與振盪流影響；不能由單一參數宣告侵蝕深度，亦不能跳過黏性細料與非黏性砂的不同機制。","textEn":"Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale. The Shields parameter nondimensionalizes forcing; onset also depends on grading, bed form and oscillatory motion.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「床面剪力無因次化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dimensionless bed shear\" is correct?","options":["潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b286-v15-22","title":"床面剪力無因次化：定量估算","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「床面剪力無因次化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dimensionless bed shear” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「床面剪力無因次化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dimensionless bed shear\", which statement holds?","options":["覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b286-v15-23","title":"床面剪力無因次化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「床面剪力無因次化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dimensionless bed shear” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth.","failure":"注意干擾：將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。","textEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。","textEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「床面剪力無因次化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dimensionless bed shear\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b286-v15-24","title":"床面剪力無因次化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「床面剪力無因次化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dimensionless bed shear” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。錯誤起動判斷可能使原本穩定的基床保護假設突然失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. Incorrect onset interpretation may invalidate the assumed stability of the bed supporting or protecting the structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。錯誤起動判斷可能使原本穩定的基床保護假設突然失效。","textEn":"Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. Incorrect onset interpretation may invalidate the assumed stability of the bed supporting or protecting the structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「床面剪力無因次化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dimensionless bed shear\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b286-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「淺水傳播時間」與「離岸幾何與岸線」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shallow-water propagation time\" and \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-25","title":"淺水傳播時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「淺水傳播時間」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shallow-water propagation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。這個近似不適用任意短波，亦未計底摩擦或水流影響；地形改變既影響速度也可能造成反射，因此傳播時間只是辨識訊號因果的一項線索。 假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「淺水傳播時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure. The approximation does not apply to arbitrary short waves and excludes friction and currents. Bathymetric changes affect speed and reflections, so travel time is only one clue for interpreting cause and effect in observations. Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shallow-water propagation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「淺水傳播時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shallow-water propagation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-25-k1","title":"淺水傳播時間","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time","text":"長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。這個近似不適用任意短波，亦未計底摩擦或水流影響；地形改變既影響速度也可能造成反射，因此傳播時間只是辨識訊號因果的一項線索。","textEn":"For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure. The approximation does not apply to arbitrary short waves and excludes friction and currents.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「淺水傳播時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shallow-water propagation time\" is correct?","options":["所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。","長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.","For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b286-v15-26","title":"淺水傳播時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「淺水傳播時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shallow-water propagation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「淺水傳播時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shallow-water propagation time\", which statement holds?","options":["模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b286-v15-27","title":"淺水傳播時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「淺水傳播時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shallow-water propagation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag.","failure":"注意干擾：儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。","textEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。","textEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「淺水傳播時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shallow-water propagation time\"?","options":["使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b286-v15-28","title":"淺水傳播時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「淺水傳播時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shallow-water propagation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。把相關性峰值自動解釋為同一波列，還可能忽略反射訊號的替代來源。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. Automatically interpreting a correlation peak as one traveling wave can also overlook reflections as an alternative signal source. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。把相關性峰值自動解釋為同一波列，還可能忽略反射訊號的替代來源。","textEn":"Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. Automatically interpreting a correlation peak as one traveling wave can also overlook reflections as an alternative signal source.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「淺水傳播時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shallow-water propagation time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b286-v15-29","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「離岸幾何與岸線」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。幾何比例可以整理案例，不能直接預報連島砂洲或突出灘形成；功能比較還需確認結構淹水狀態及尺度，避免將出水防波堤經驗直接移植到潛堤。 假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「離岸幾何與岸線」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response. A geometric ratio organizes comparisons; it does not directly predict a salient or tombolo. Comparisons must account for submergence and scale rather than transferring emerged-breakwater experience directly to a submerged structure in a different sediment regime. Assume length100m and offshore distance200m. L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「離岸幾何與岸線」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Offshore geometry and shoreline response”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-29-k1","title":"離岸幾何與岸線","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response","text":"堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。幾何比例可以整理案例，不能直接預報連島砂洲或突出灘形成；功能比較還需確認結構淹水狀態及尺度，避免將出水防波堤經驗直接移植到潛堤。","textEn":"Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response. A geometric ratio organizes comparisons; it does not directly predict a salient or tombolo.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「離岸幾何與岸線」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\" is correct?","options":["堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。"],"optionsEn":["The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response."],"answer":2,"explanation":"堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b286-v15-30","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：定量估算","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「離岸幾何與岸線」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length100m and offshore distance200m. L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length100m and offshore distance200m. L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「離岸幾何與岸線」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b286-v15-31","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「離岸幾何與岸線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study.","failure":"注意干擾：某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。","textEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。","textEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「離岸幾何與岸線」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b286-v15-32","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：失效診斷","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「離岸幾何與岸線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。只憑幾何比例許諾岸線效果，會忽略整段海岸的收支限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. Geometry-only promises therefore ignore sediment-budget limitations across the wider coast and its changing wave climate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。只憑幾何比例許諾岸線效果，會忽略整段海岸的收支限制。","textEn":"Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. Geometry-only promises therefore ignore sediment-budget limitations across the wider coast and its changing wave climate.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「離岸幾何與岸線」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b286-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「堤頂沉陷與覆水」與「數值步長與收斂」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Crest settlement and water cover\" and \"Numerical timestep and convergence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-33","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「堤頂沉陷與覆水」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crest settlement and water cover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。局部差異沉陷還形成優先過流通道，而透射對幾何的反應通常非線性；需要把結構監測、水位歷程與水理測試放在同一狀態描述中追蹤。 假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堤頂沉陷與覆水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume. Differential movement also creates preferred flow paths, while transmission often responds nonlinearly to geometry. Structural surveys, water-level history and hydraulic observations therefore need to describe the same evolving state; a percentage change in cover cannot determine an equal change in transmission. Assume fixed water level and original cover0.8m. Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crest settlement and water cover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crest settlement and water cover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-33-k1","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover","text":"潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。局部差異沉陷還形成優先過流通道，而透射對幾何的反應通常非線性；需要把結構監測、水位歷程與水理測試放在同一狀態描述中追蹤。","textEn":"Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume. Differential movement also creates preferred flow paths, while transmission often responds nonlinearly to geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堤頂沉陷與覆水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crest settlement and water cover\" is correct?","options":["潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b286-v15-34","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：定量估算","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crest settlement and water cover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed water level and original cover0.8m. Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed water level and original cover0.8m. Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crest settlement and water cover\", which statement holds?","options":["波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b286-v15-35","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「堤頂沉陷與覆水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crest settlement and water cover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels.","failure":"注意干擾：量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。","textEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。","textEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堤頂沉陷與覆水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crest settlement and water cover\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b286-v15-36","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crest settlement and water cover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。不同潮位的透射資料若直接比較，則可能把水位造成的差別誤認為結構損壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. Comparing transmission at different tides can instead mistake a water-level effect for deterioration of the physical structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。不同潮位的透射資料若直接比較，則可能把水位造成的差別誤認為結構損壞。","textEn":"Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. Comparing transmission at different tides can instead mistake a water-level effect for deterioration of the physical structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堤頂沉陷與覆水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crest settlement and water cover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b286-v15-37","title":"數值步長與收斂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「數值步長與收斂」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Numerical timestep and convergence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。特徵速度限制顯式步長，但邊界、乾濕轉換及所用格式可能更嚴；網格與步長應分別細化，並保持物理邊界一致，才能分辨數值擴散與真實地形平滑。 假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「數值步長與收斂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence. Characteristic speed constrains an explicit timestep, while boundaries, wetting and drying or the selected scheme may be more restrictive. Refine space and time separately under unchanged physical boundaries to distinguish numerical diffusion from genuine smoothing of coastal terrain. Assume a one-dimensional explicit shallow-water illustration: U=2m/s,h=2m,Δt=0.5s,Δx=5m. C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Numerical timestep and convergence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「數值步長與收斂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Numerical timestep and convergence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-37-k1","title":"數值步長與收斂","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence","text":"地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。特徵速度限制顯式步長，但邊界、乾濕轉換及所用格式可能更嚴；網格與步長應分別細化，並保持物理邊界一致，才能分辨數值擴散與真實地形平滑。","textEn":"A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence. Characteristic speed constrains an explicit timestep, while boundaries, wetting and drying or the selected scheme may be more restrictive.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「數值步長與收斂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Numerical timestep and convergence\" is correct?","options":["模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。","地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.","A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b286-v15-38","title":"數值步長與收斂：定量估算","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「數值步長與收斂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Numerical timestep and convergence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a one-dimensional explicit shallow-water illustration: U=2m/s,h=2m,Δt=0.5s,Δx=5m. C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a one-dimensional explicit shallow-water illustration: U=2m/s,h=2m,Δt=0.5s,Δx=5m. C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「數值步長與收斂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Numerical timestep and convergence\", which statement holds?","options":["只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b286-v15-39","title":"數值步長與收斂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「數值步長與收斂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Numerical timestep and convergence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps.","failure":"注意干擾：平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。","textEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。","textEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「數值步長與收斂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Numerical timestep and convergence\"?","options":["逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b286-v15-40","title":"數值步長與收斂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「數值步長與收斂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Numerical timestep and convergence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。圖像平滑不代表守恆正確，錯誤地形趨勢甚至可能看起來很合理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. Smooth graphics do not establish conservation, and an incorrect morphological trend can still appear visually plausible to an uncritical observer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。圖像平滑不代表守恆正確，錯誤地形趨勢甚至可能看起來很合理。","textEn":"A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. Smooth graphics do not establish conservation, and an incorrect morphological trend can still appear visually plausible to an uncritical observer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「數值步長與收斂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Numerical timestep and convergence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
